    "result_text": "The full test suite consists of just the `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are the base class and a helper), and it passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature so the app satisfies the spec and the test suite is green.\n\n**What the spec required:** when a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, allow an owner at an address already used by a same-lastName owner, assign both owners the same stable `householdId`, and return it.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` string property to the `Owner` response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` and the MapStruct mapper pick it up automatically; `OwnerFieldsDto`/input is unaffected since it's read-only).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table. Tests run against `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in the schema script.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Replaced the old `rejectDuplicateHousehold` with `applyHousehold`, which:\n   - Finds existing owners in the same household (normalized case-insensitive lastName + address match, as before).\n   - If none match, does nothing; if a match exists but `sharesHousehold` isn't `true`, still throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409) \u2014 preserving prior behavior.\n   - If `sharesHousehold` is `true`, derives a **stable, deterministic** `householdId` (`HH-` + first 12 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over the normalized `lastName|address` key), assigns it to the new owner, and backfills any existing household members with the same value.\n\nBecause `householdId` is a pure function of the normalized household key, every joiner independently derives the identical value \u2014 so owners `b` and `c` in the test share the same non-blank `householdId`, satisfying `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`.",
